{"id": "EUVD-2026-94449", "enisaUuid": "7dd15a33-aaf2-3ee2-b376-08ec16ee3506", "description": "A vulnerability in Cisco NX-OS Software could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to exhaust system resources, causing a denial of service (DoS) condition.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability exists because rate limiting was improperly applied to some protocols. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a high rate of UDP or TCP connections to a data plane interface on an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause instability to various routing and control plane protocols through some packet loss and temporary disruptions, causing a DoS condition. This DoS condition will clear without manual intervention soon after the high rate of traffic is stopped.", "datePublished": "2026-10-07T16:12:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T17:42:39", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-nxos-nscpdos-SnderkC7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8g9j-7mq6-rw6g", "CVE-2026-20173"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0018d2dd-e5ee-362e-b849-48a2599fdc1d", "product": {"name": "Cisco NX-OS Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "10.3(3)"}, {"id": "04d48fe0-4398-37ad-a78c-1e7b47037177", "product": {"name": "Cisco NX-OS Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "9.3(4)"}, {"id": "056b741b-6747-3989-afbd-b5899f11bd2b", "product": {"name": "Cisco NX-OS Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "8.2(2)"}, {"id": "06bf46f1-6db6-33de-8fbc-7f92fb6479b1", "product": {"name": "Cisco NX-OS Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "8.3(1)"}, {"id": "0be4a944-e266-34a3-a83d-cb2efa92064f", "product": {"name": "Cisco NX-OS Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "9.3(14)"}, {"id": "0cc2550c-fa81